{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "08J7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\to\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0002": "$K, L$", "MATH_0003": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nRf_*R\\SheafHom(L, K) \\longrightarrow R\\SheafHom(Rf_*L, Rf_*K)\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$Rf_*R\\SheafHom(L, K) \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D}}^\\mathbf{L} Rf_*L\n\\to Rf_*K$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nRf_*R\\SheafHom(L, K) \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D}}^\\mathbf{L} Rf_*L \\to\nRf_*(R\\SheafHom(L, K) \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}}^\\mathbf{L} L) \\to\nRf_*K\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$Rf_*$", "MATH_0008": "$R\\SheafHom(L, K) \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}}^\\mathbf{L} L \\to K$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-internal-hom}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{remark-cup-product}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-internal-hom-composition}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-projection-formula-for-internal-hom}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d89e0848e8fd51dc8e3498fa5e9e8efb465a7d7034f7808e2da8d191447ae12e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5247426f01e3058cb1bc18093dc545d86bc2f8017fad99beeb8edd19fc285597", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of ringed topoi.\nLet <MATH_0002> be objects of <MATH_0003>. We claim there is\na canonical map\n<MATH_0004>\nNamely, by (<REF_0001>) this is the same thing\nas a map\n<MATH_0005>.\nFor this we can use the composition\n<MATH_0006>\nwhere the first arrow is the relative cup product\n(Remark <REF_0002>) and the second arrow is <MATH_0007> applied\nto the canonical map\n<MATH_0008>\ncoming from Lemma <REF_0003>\n(with <MATH_0009> in one of the spots).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5211bffff20fd7f9be9d8276e70fa5a7444020ffff422960363177c2d96ca943", "unit_id": "tag:0B6D:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "08J7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$h : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}) \\to (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}'), \\mathcal{O}')$", "MATH_0002": "$K, L$", "MATH_0003": "$D(\\mathcal{O}')$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nLh^*R\\SheafHom(K, L) \\longrightarrow R\\SheafHom(Lh^*K, Lh^*L)\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nLh^*R\\SheafHom(K, L) \\otimes^\\mathbf{L} Lh^*K \\longrightarrow Lh^*L\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$Lh^*(\\SheafHom(K, L) \\otimes^\\mathbf{L} K)$", "MATH_0008": "$$\nR\\SheafHom(K, L) \\otimes^\\mathbf{L} K \\longrightarrow L.\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\text{id} :\nR\\SheafHom(K, L)\n\\longrightarrow\nR\\SheafHom(K, L)\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-internal-hom}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-internal-hom}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-tensor-product}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{equation-internal-hom}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-prepare-fancy-base-change}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d18f34c2bb5098fbe12e7893514607204bfd16729fd0710ea08fc73320168307", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:523a44d77ccca3846067113a99f1f50df5712b194048631092c03afa6a734f42", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe a morphism of ringed topoi. Let <MATH_0002> be objects of <MATH_0003>.\nWe claim there is a canonical map\n<MATH_0004>\nin <MATH_0005>. Namely, by (<REF_0001>)\nproved in Lemma <REF_0002>\nsuch a map is the same thing as a map\n<MATH_0006>\nThe source of this arrow is <MATH_0007>\nby Lemma <REF_0003>\nhence it suffices to construct a canonical map\n<MATH_0008>\nFor this we take the arrow corresponding to\n<MATH_0009>\nvia (<REF_0004>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:680020a8e6a16687a3e233f0be02c0fd57fda648557dc27d3f23312a64dded7b", "unit_id": "tag:08JF:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "08J7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}'), \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{C}'})\n\\ar[r]_h \\ar[d]_{f'} &\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\ar[d]^f \\\\\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}'), \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{D}'})\n\\ar[r]^g &\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$K, L$", "MATH_0003": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nLg^*Rf_*R\\SheafHom(K, L)\n\\longrightarrow\nR(f')_*R\\SheafHom(Lh^*K, Lh^*L)\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{D}'})$", "MATH_0006": "\\begin{align*}\nL(f')^*Lg^*Rf_*R\\SheafHom(K, L)\n& =\nLh^*Lf^*Rf_*R\\SheafHom(K, L) \\\\\n& \\to\nLh^*R\\SheafHom(K, L) \\\\\n& \\to\nR\\SheafHom(Lh^*K, Lh^*L)\n\\end{align*}", "MATH_0007": "$Lf^*Rf_* \\to \\text{id}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-prepare-fancy-base-change}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-fancy-base-change}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:60d24979c548df8dc724c37b59a547f6b38a2ce59f4795c7f4ec80ee59b2729c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6ed6343c09f7209c526f2c863a97068592d86fe594fdd335e3e983da30e4d9e5", "source_text": "Suppose that\n<MATH_0001>\nis a commutative diagram of ringed topoi. Let <MATH_0002> be objects\nof <MATH_0003>. We claim there exists a canonical base change\nmap\n<MATH_0004>\nin <MATH_0005>. Namely, we take the map adjoint to\nthe composition\n<MATH_0006>\nwhere the first arrow uses the adjunction mapping\n<MATH_0007> and the second arrow is the canonical map\nconstructed in Remark <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4bb9e1c078a2c3fd5d9d2cbea42b97ed42677112f19778a314e4e7c8f9591a46", "unit_id": "tag:08JG:statement"}
